## 4. Obligations of the requester

The requester agrees to:

1. Use the data only for the purpose described in §2.
2. Not attempt to re-identify any individual whose data appears in
   the dataset, whether directly or through linkage attack.
3. Maintain the data under access controls equivalent to those
   required by the host's IRB or equivalent ethics body.
4. Cite the dataset in any resulting publication per the host's
   preferred citation form (provided separately on the dataset
   landing page).
5. Report any actual or suspected security incident affecting the
   dataset to the host within 72 hours of discovery, consistent
   with GDPR Article 33 notification obligations where applicable.
6. Destroy the data within {{dataset.retentionDays}} days of project
   completion, or sooner upon written request from the host.

## 5. Publication and pre-publication review

The requester will provide the host with **at least 30 days'
notice** before submission of any manuscript that uses the dataset.
The host may not block publication, but may request:

- correction of factual errors regarding the dataset's provenance,
- a citation form change,
- redaction of any inadvertently-included identifying detail.

## 6. Liability and warranty

The dataset is provided "as is", without warranty of completeness,
accuracy, or fitness for any particular purpose. The host's
liability for any consequence of the requester's use of the data
is limited to the maximum extent permitted by applicable law.

## 7. Term and termination

This agreement is effective from the date above and continues until
all data has been destroyed under §4(6), unless terminated earlier
by either party in writing. The obligations under §4(2) and §4(5)
survive termination indefinitely.

## 8. Governing law

This agreement is governed by the law of the host institution's
primary place of establishment. Disputes are subject to the
exclusive jurisdiction of that court.

